- [medium] bycontrol-route-shadowing: /ssp-export-offerings/by-control/:controlId shares a prefix
  with /ssp-export-offerings/:id, and ByControl was only ever exercised by calling the handler
  directly — so a router that resolved :id first would have sent "by-control" to GetByID and
  failed with "invalid offering id", silently, with both routes still registered and both
  reachable in isolation. Added TestByControlRouteIsNotShadowedByGetByID, which drives the real
  echo router and pins both dispatches. (Echo does prefer the static segment; the test guarantees
  it stays that way.)
- Also pinned: a by-component with no implementation-status must not gain an empty {"state": ""}
  from a PUT that omits it (asserted in the blind-Save regression test).
